# @cosyte/terminology

A zero-dependency terminology engine for US healthcare code systems. It is not a wire parser: it
mirrors the FHIR Terminology Module (`$translate`, `$lookup`, `$validate-code`, `$expand`) over FHIR
resources and standard releases you supply, and it never fabricates a code.

## When to use it

- "What system is OID 2.16.840.1.113883.6.1", "normalize this code system identifier".
- "Translate this code with our ConceptMap", "is this mapping 1:1 or 1:many".
- Load LOINC CSV, RxNorm or UMLS RRF, the ICD-10-CM order file or a FHIR CodeSystem, then look up a
  display or check a code (deprecated and not-billable status carried through).
- Expand a ValueSet, or decide whether a coding is in one.
- "Is `mg/dl` valid UCUM", "are `mmol/L` and `mmol.L-1` the same unit".
- ICD-9-CM to ICD-10-CM (or back) with the CMS GEM files; SNOMED CT to ICD-10-CM with the NLM
  complex map.
- RxNorm: ingredients of a drug, generic for a brand, NDC to RXCUI.

Use another skill when:

- Reading or validating FHIR resources: `cosyte-fhir` (it takes a terminology service you implement).
- Reading a C-CDA document: `cosyte-ccda` (its code systems page,
  https://docs.cosyte.com/ccda/code-systems, says its `TerminologyAdapter` mirrors this engine, so
  you can wire the engine in behind it).
- You are converting HL7 v2 to FHIR: `cosyte-transform`.

## Install

```bash
npm install @cosyte/terminology
```

Zero runtime dependencies (Node standard library only). Dual ESM and CJS, built with `tsup` and
checked with `attw`. Node.js 22 or later, tested on 22, 24 and 26. Runnable programs are in the
repository's `examples/` folder.

## Minimal example

```ts
import { isUnknownSystem, loadCodeSystem, loadConceptMap, lookup, resolveSystem } from "@cosyte/terminology";
import { translate, ucumEqual, validateUcum } from "@cosyte/terminology";

// 1. Resolve an OID, a mnemonic or a URI to the canonical system URI.
const loinc = resolveSystem("2.16.840.1.113883.6.1");
console.log(isUnknownSystem(loinc) ? "unknown" : loinc.url);

// 2. $translate through a ConceptMap you supply (an inline example map here).
const map = loadConceptMap({
  resourceType: "ConceptMap",
  url: "http://example.org/cm/gender",
  group: [
    {
      source: "http://hl7.org/fhir/administrative-gender",
      target: "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v2-0001",
      element: [{ code: "male", target: [{ code: "M", equivalence: "equivalent" }] }],
    },
  ],
});
const result = translate({ system: "http://hl7.org/fhir/administrative-gender", code: "male" }, map);
if (result.unmapped) {
  console.log("unmapped", result.mode); // a typed outcome, never a guessed target
} else {
  for (const match of result.matches) console.log(match.target.code, match.equivalence);
}

// 3. $lookup in a code system you load (a tiny FHIR CodeSystem here).
const cs = loadCodeSystem({
  format: "fhir",
  resource: {
    resourceType: "CodeSystem",
    url: "http://example.org/cs",
    concept: [{ code: "a", display: "Alpha" }],
  },
});
const hit = lookup(cs, "a");
console.log(hit.found ? hit.display : hit.code);
console.log(lookup(cs, "zz").found); // an unknown code is TERM_CODE_UNKNOWN, never a made-up display

// 4. UCUM recognition and canonicalization only: no magnitude conversion.
console.log(validateUcum("mmol/L").valid, ucumEqual("N", "kg.m/s2"), ucumEqual("mg", "g"));
```

Expected output. Most lines are values the README asserts; the rest follow from the type
declarations. We have not run this exact snippet.

```text
http://loinc.org
M equivalent
Alpha
false
true true false
```

## Key API

- `resolveSystem(id)`, `isUnknownSystem`, `SYSTEM_IDENTITIES`.
- `loadConceptMap(json)`, `translate(coding, map)`: matches, or a typed `TERM_TRANSLATE_UNMAPPED`.
- `loadCodeSystem(source)` (`format` `"rrf"`, `"csv"`, `"fixed-width"`, `"fhir"`), `lookup`,
  `validateCode`.
- `loadValueSet(json)`, `expand(vs, ctx?)`, `validateCodeInValueSet(coding, vs, ctx?)`.
- `validateUcum(unit)`, `ucumEqual(a, b)`.
- `loadGems`, `applyGem` (`invertGem` always throws); `loadComplexMap`, `applyComplexMap`.
- `loadRxNormGraph`, `ingredientsOf`, `genericFor`, `brandsFor`, `doseFormsOf`, `consistsOf`,
  `resolveNdc`, `approximateMatch` (opt-in, results marked `approximate: true`).
- `TerminologyError` (`code` from `FATAL_CODES`) for unusable input; `DIAGNOSTIC_CODES` for typed
  outcomes and load warnings.

## Limits and known defects

We have no known defects on record for 0.1.7. The README states these limits:

- **No code-system release is bundled.** SNOMED CT, CPT, LOINC, UMLS/RxNorm, the CMS GEM files, the
  NLM complex-map refset and VSAC value sets are bring-your-own, under their steward's terms. The
  RxNorm Prescribable Content and ICD-10-CM content packs are not bundled either. Do not tell a user
  a lookup works until they supply the release.
- **What is bundled:** the UCUM table (`ucum-essence.xml` version 2.2, revision-date 2024-06-17,
  copyright Regenstrief Institute, reproduced verbatim under the UCUM licence, notice at
  `vendor/ucum/NOTICE.md`); code-system identity facts (`SYSTEM_IDENTITIES`); the SNOMED CT
  concepts the crosswalk resolver names (`MAP_CATEGORIES` and two gender findings); RxNorm
  relationship and term-type names (`RELA`, `RELA_INVERSE`, `TERM_TYPES`). Some SNOMED CT, ICD-10-CM
  and RxNorm identifiers also appear in API documentation examples.
- No UCUM magnitude conversion (`mg/dL` to `mmol/L` is refused). Case-sensitive UCUM only; a
  case-insensitive spelling is `TERM_UCUM_INVALID`.
- Maps are never inverted: load the other-direction GEM file instead. Unmapped and unknown results
  are typed, never guessed; a 1:many map returns every candidate, so do not pick one silently.
- `expand` can return `complete: false` (then `contains` is a lower bound), and
  `validateCodeInValueSet` can return `undetermined: true` rather than a fabricated `false`.
- RxNorm is navigated along authored edges only: an `SCD` has no ingredient edge (use `consistsOf`,
  then `ingredientsOf`). Read the `tty` of every result.
- Conformance claims are partial (ValueSet: 20 of 101 HL7 ecosystem cases passed, 81 declined;
  UCUM: validation and conversion case kinds only). Details and other limits are in
  [references/REFERENCE.md](https://github.com/cosyte/agent-skills/blob/main/skills/cosyte-terminology/references/REFERENCE.md).

## PHI handling

The engine holds code systems, not patient records, but the codes you ask about can be PHI in
context.

- Diagnostic `message`, `detail`, `reason` and `err.stack` text is value-free: nothing you configured
  or loaded reaches it. A locus (line number, column count, index path) sits beside it.
- Result objects are different: a typed unknown or unmapped outcome names the code, unit or NDC you
  asked about. Log the `code` and the locus, not the whole result.
- `applyComplexMap` can take a `PatientContext` (`ageYears`, `gender`); treat what you pass in as
  PHI in your own code.
- Use synthetic codes and contexts in tests and examples. Never paste real patient data into prompts,
  fixtures or logs.

